Z||000016||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-18-2001||04:00 PM||||I wanted a Fiero since I was 13 (1984).  I have the car I wanted now (since December 24, 2000).<P>Everytime I go out and work on the car, it gets better.  When I work on my truck, it just contiues to run the same (like new).  So, I get a reward for my labor with my Fiero.  This could never occur if I work on my wife's '98 Mazda 626.<P>My 1984 sport coupe looks like no other car out there.  It's totally unique.  It's as unusual as a Kharman Ghia but with better handling, more room inside, better sytling, and more power.  The car looks like it's 3ft tall and a mile wide (1988 Formula wheels help with the wide-track look).  <P>I go "nuts" over my Fiero, because there's no denying that I saved it from the scrap yard and it saved me from watching hundreds of hours of TV.  <P>We need each other.  And, after lots of time and money, people compliment me on my cool little car.  I grin like a proud father would thinking my love for my Fiero has changed someone's mind about these irresistable machines.  <P>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 03-18-2001).]<P>Edits are to fix spelling errors . . .<p>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000017||88formula||03-18-2001||07:15 PM||||Good answers! I know why you guys are nuts over these cars because I am too. Just look at my 1145 posts. I was just looking for some creative answers or I just wanted to see what you guys would have said. <P>HUH!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
