Z||000020||EXHIBITER||03-19-2001||01:58 AM||||Hey, has anybody noticed that whenever you see another fiero drive by you freak out (or go nuts) but when you're getting a ride in someone else's car (that's not a fiero) they don't even flinch when they see their same kind of car drive by?<P>88formula: I'm never going to hear the end of it...HUH! he he he  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000021||Conrad Sanville||03-19-2001||08:10 AM||||I went nuts the first time I saw spy shots of the Pcar back in the early eighties.  The low, wide stance, the laid back windshield and the flexible body panels were the features that grabbed my attention.<P>I was at the Art Center College of Design in CA studying transportation design when the Fiero was in development.  The prospects of GM introducing that type of car during the great sales slump back then generated a lot of excitement in the design community.  The general consensus was why did it take so long for an American carmaker to perceive and fill that gap in the marketplace.<P>I was working at a local GM dealership in Northern Vermont when the first batch of Fieros we ordered came off the truck. It was quite an event!  Especially when my white '84 was on it.  It was a day I will never forget...I still have that car...Almost 18 years and 345k miles later...Since then I have picked up an '86GT and a low mileage '85 SE.  The '85 is my daily driver and with 4 good snow tires, its mid-engine configuration and plastic body panels make it a great winter car!<P>The Fiero is one of the world's most unique cars...In spite of its common mechanicals.  Over time I have come to appreciate the car's flexible dingproof corrosion resistant body panels.  I am also glad that they ceased production of the car.  This way they the Fiero is once again enjoying that fact that they are truly exclusive as they were in the fall of '83   <P>    ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Jake2m4||03-19-2001||05:00 PM||||To tell you the truth, I didn't even know what a fiero was 2 years ago (I first saw one when I was 16, I'm 18 now).  But, once I saw one up close I knew I had to have one.  Its just an awesome car.||||reg||1
